  "label": "The text 'wing wing wing' is mapped onto the man's phone call scene, implying the sound he is making or hearing.",
  "description": "The textual phrase 'wing wing wing' is overlaid on the image and is directly associated with the visual of the man on the phone. The mapping suggests that the sound effect is being projected onto the phone call context — either the man is making this sound, or he is hearing it. This creates an analogical mapping where the nonsensical text is mapped onto the auditory experience implied by the visual of the phone conversation. The humor arises from the incongruity between the serious visual context and the childish sound effect.",
